0. What it is?
You can use this script to parse system call chain and generate system call graph and call report automatically.
It also support rich overwrite features such as call chain node/edge rename/combine/regroup/delete.

1. Installation
You should have python3 installed with pip and virtualenv support.
You should have graphviz installed. (brew update && brew install graphviz)

cd your_working_dir
virtualenv callchain
cd callchain
source bin/activate
pip install -r requirement.txt

2. Usage

Go to src folder first:
cd ./src

You should define your own business scenario in scenario.py (following existing definitions, should be straight-forward).
You may want to add your own parsing rules in scenario.py (for scenario specific cases) or define.py (for common cases). All rules are indeed regular expressions and should be straight-forward.
You should modify callchain.py to parse your scenario and use your own output folder.

Then run:
python callchain.py

Get results from your defined output folder and you may want to add more customizations to the graph and report. The re-run the script.

3. Generated files
callchain.dot			the graph dot file
callchain.dot.svg		the exported dot graph in svg file
calls.report.txt		the exported API call report
original_callchain.txt	the original callchain file
original_calls.txt		the original API call file
refined_callchain.txt	the refined callchain file used to generate the dot graph
refined_calls.txt		the refined API call file used to generate the API call report
